<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Interactive on OLIVER GIDDINGS</title><link>https://example.org/tags/interactive/</link><description>Recent content in Interactive on OLIVER GIDDINGS</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/tags/interactive/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>DOT PRODUCT - Interactive Explorer</title><link>https://example.org/post/dot-product-explorer/</link><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/post/dot-product-explorer/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="dot-product">DOT PRODUCT
&lt;/h1>&lt;p>The dot product is often introduced as a list of numbers. This experiment shows its geometric meaning: &lt;strong>how much of one vector points in the direction of another&lt;/strong>.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Drag the sliders, rotate the scene, and watch the projection and formula update together.&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab" data-dot-product-lab>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__header">
&lt;div>
&lt;span class="dot-product-lab__eyebrow">Interactive linear algebra&lt;/span>
&lt;h2>See the projection&lt;/h2>
&lt;/div>
&lt;button class="dot-product-lab__button" type="button" data-action="reset">Reset view&lt;/button>
&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__layout">
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__stage">
&lt;canvas data-canvas aria-label="Interactive three-dimensional dot product visualization">&lt;/canvas>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__hint">Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;aside class="dot-product-lab__controls">
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__result-label">Current dot product&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__result" data-result>0.00&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__formula" data-formula>a · b = |a||b|cos(θ)&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__meaning" data-meaning>Positive: b has a component in the direction of a.&lt;/div>
&lt;label class="dot-product-lab__control">
&lt;span>&lt;b>Length of a&lt;/b>&lt;output data-a-value>2.00&lt;/output>&lt;/span>
&lt;input data-a type="range" min="0.4" max="3" step="0.05" value="2">
&lt;/label>
&lt;label class="dot-product-lab__control">
&lt;span>&lt;b>Length of b&lt;/b>&lt;output data-b-value>1.60&lt;/output>&lt;/span>
&lt;input data-b type="range" min="0.4" max="3" step="0.05" value="1.6">
&lt;/label>
&lt;label class="dot-product-lab__control">
&lt;span>&lt;b>Angle θ&lt;/b>&lt;output data-angle-value>55°&lt;/output>&lt;/span>
&lt;input data-angle type="range" min="0" max="180" step="1" value="55">
&lt;/label>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__presets">
&lt;span>Try a preset&lt;/span>
&lt;div>
&lt;button type="button" data-preset="0">Same direction&lt;/button>
&lt;button type="button" data-preset="90">Perpendicular&lt;/button>
&lt;button type="button" data-preset="180">Opposite direction&lt;/button>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;button class="dot-product-lab__play" type="button" data-action="play">Play angle animation&lt;/button>
&lt;/aside>
&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__steps">
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__step is-active" data-step="0">&lt;span>01&lt;/span>&lt;b>Two vectors&lt;/b>&lt;small>a and b start at the same origin.&lt;/small>&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__step" data-step="1">&lt;span>02&lt;/span>&lt;b>Project b onto a&lt;/b>&lt;small>The green line is the useful component.&lt;/small>&lt;/div>
&lt;div class="dot-product-lab__step" data-step="2">&lt;span>03&lt;/span>&lt;b>Read the sign&lt;/b>&lt;small>Acute is positive, right is zero, obtuse is negative.&lt;/small>&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;h2 id="the-idea-in-one-line">The idea in one line
&lt;/h2>&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>a · b = |a||b|cos(θ)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>The green projection is the geometric part that the dot product measures. When the angle is less than 90°, the projection points along &lt;strong>a&lt;/strong> and the result is positive. At 90° the projection disappears. Past 90° it points backwards and the result becomes negative.&lt;/p>
&lt;script>
(function () {
const lab = document.querySelector('[data-dot-product-lab]');
if (!lab) return;
const canvas = lab.querySelector('[data-canvas]');
const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
const aInput = lab.querySelector('[data-a]');
const bInput = lab.querySelector('[data-b]');
const angleInput = lab.querySelector('[data-angle]');
const result = lab.querySelector('[data-result]');
const formula = lab.querySelector('[data-formula]');
const meaning = lab.querySelector('[data-meaning]');
const aValue = lab.querySelector('[data-a-value]');
const bValue = lab.querySelector('[data-b-value]');
const angleValue = lab.querySelector('[data-angle-value]');
const playButton = lab.querySelector('[data-action="play"]');
const state = { a: 2, b: 1.6, angle: 55, yaw: -0.7, pitch: 0.55, zoom: 1, playing: false, lastTime: 0 };
const colors = { text: '#f5f7fb', muted: '#a9b2c1', grid: '#2a313c', axis: '#687486', a: '#6ea8ff', b: '#ff8668', projection: '#54d6ae', angle: '#f1bd5b' };
function resize() {
const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
const width = Math.max(1, Math.round(rect.width));
const height = Math.max(1, Math.round(rect.height));
canvas.width = width;
canvas.height = height;
ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
draw();
}
function project(vector) {
const cy = Math.cos(state.yaw);
const sy = Math.sin(state.yaw);
const cp = Math.cos(state.pitch);
const sp = Math.sin(state.pitch);
const x = vector.x * cy + vector.z * sy;
const z = -vector.x * sy + vector.z * cy;
const y = vector.y * cp - z * sp;
return { x, y, depth: vector.y * sp + z * cp };
}
function point(vector, width, height) {
const p = project(vector);
const scale = Math.min(width, height) * 0.18 * state.zoom;
return { x: width * 0.5 + p.x * scale, y: height * 0.5 - p.y * scale, depth: p.depth };
}
function vectorLine(from, to, color, width, dashed) {
ctx.save();
ctx.strokeStyle = color;
ctx.lineWidth = width;
ctx.setLineDash(dashed ? [6, 5] : []);
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(from.x, from.y);
ctx.lineTo(to.x, to.y);
ctx.stroke();
ctx.setLineDash([]);
const angle = Math.atan2(to.y - from.y, to.x - from.x);
const size = dashed ? 7 : 10;
ctx.fillStyle = color;
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(to.x, to.y);
ctx.lineTo(to.x - size * Math.cos(angle - 0.45), to.y - size * Math.sin(angle - 0.45));
ctx.lineTo(to.x - size * Math.cos(angle + 0.45), to.y - size * Math.sin(angle + 0.45));
ctx.closePath();
ctx.fill();
ctx.restore();
}
function label(text, x, y, color) {
ctx.save();
ctx.font = '500 14px system-ui, sans-serif';
ctx.fillStyle = color;
ctx.fillText(text, x + 8, y - 8);
ctx.restore();
}
function drawGrid(width, height) {
const range = 3.2;
for (let i = -6; i &lt;= 6; i += 1) {
const x1 = point({ x: -range, y: 0, z: i * 0.5 }, width, height);
const x2 = point({ x: range, y: 0, z: i * 0.5 }, width, height);
const y1 = point({ x: i * 0.5, y: 0, z: -range }, width, height);
const y2 = point({ x: i * 0.5, y: 0, z: range }, width, height);
ctx.strokeStyle = colors.grid;
ctx.lineWidth = 1;
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(x1.x, x1.y);
ctx.lineTo(x2.x, x2.y);
ctx.moveTo(y1.x, y1.y);
ctx.lineTo(y2.x, y2.y);
ctx.stroke();
}
}
function drawAngle(origin, endA, endB) {
const start = Math.atan2(endA.y - origin.y, endA.x - origin.x);
const end = Math.atan2(endB.y - origin.y, endB.x - origin.x);
let delta = end - start;
while (delta > Math.PI) delta -= Math.PI * 2;
while (delta &lt; -Math.PI) delta += Math.PI * 2;
ctx.save();
ctx.strokeStyle = colors.angle;
ctx.lineWidth = 2;
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.arc(origin.x, origin.y, 42, start, start + delta, delta &lt; 0);
ctx.stroke();
ctx.font = '500 13px system-ui, sans-serif';
ctx.fillStyle = colors.angle;
ctx.fillText('θ', origin.x + Math.cos(start + delta * 0.5) * 53, origin.y + Math.sin(start + delta * 0.5) * 53);
ctx.restore();
}
function draw() {
const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
const width = rect.width;
const height = rect.height;
if (!width || !height) return;
ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);
drawGrid(width, height);
const origin = point({ x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 }, width, height);
const rad = state.angle * Math.PI / 180;
const av = { x: state.a, y: 0, z: 0 };
const bv = { x: state.b * Math.cos(rad), y: state.b * Math.sin(rad), z: 0 };
const projection = { x: state.a * state.b * Math.cos(rad) / state.a, y: 0, z: 0 };
const endA = point(av, width, height);
const endB = point(bv, width, height);
const endProjection = point(projection, width, height);
ctx.strokeStyle = colors.axis;
ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
const axisX = point({ x: 3.3, y: 0, z: 0 }, width, height);
const axisY = point({ x: 0, y: 3.3, z: 0 }, width, height);
const axisZ = point({ x: 0, y: 0, z: 3.3 }, width, height);
[[axisX, 'x'], [axisY, 'y'], [axisZ, 'z']].forEach(function (item) {
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(origin.x, origin.y);
ctx.lineTo(item[0].x, item[0].y);
ctx.stroke();
label(item[1], item[0].x, item[0].y, colors.muted);
});
vectorLine(origin, endA, colors.a, 4, false);
vectorLine(origin, endB, colors.b, 4, false);
vectorLine(origin, endProjection, colors.projection, 3, false);
vectorLine(endB, endProjection, colors.projection, 2, true);
drawAngle(origin, endA, endB);
label('a', endA.x, endA.y, colors.a);
label('b', endB.x, endB.y, colors.b);
label('projₐ(b)', endProjection.x, endProjection.y, colors.projection);
ctx.fillStyle = colors.text;
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.arc(origin.x, origin.y, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
ctx.fill();
}
function updateText() {
const dot = state.a * state.b * Math.cos(state.angle * Math.PI / 180);
result.textContent = dot.toFixed(2);
formula.textContent = 'a · b = ' + state.a.toFixed(2) + ' × ' + state.b.toFixed(2) + ' × cos(' + state.angle + '°) = ' + dot.toFixed(2);
aValue.value = state.a.toFixed(2);
bValue.value = state.b.toFixed(2);
angleValue.value = state.angle + '°';
if (state.angle &lt; 89.5) {
meaning.textContent = 'Positive: b has a component in the direction of a.';
meaning.dataset.sign = 'positive';
} else if (state.angle > 90.5) {
meaning.textContent = 'Negative: b has a component opposite to the direction of a.';
meaning.dataset.sign = 'negative';
} else {
meaning.textContent = 'Zero: b is perpendicular to a, so there is no projection.';
meaning.dataset.sign = 'zero';
}
}
function syncFromInputs() {
state.a = Number(aInput.value);
state.b = Number(bInput.value);
state.angle = Number(angleInput.value);
updateText();
draw();
}
[aInput, bInput, angleInput].forEach(function (input) {
input.addEventListener('input', syncFromInputs);
});
lab.querySelectorAll('[data-preset]').forEach(function (button) {
button.addEventListener('click', function () {
angleInput.value = button.dataset.preset;
syncFromInputs();
});
});
lab.querySelector('[data-action="reset"]').addEventListener('click', function () {
state.yaw = -0.7;
state.pitch = 0.55;
state.zoom = 1;
draw();
});
playButton.addEventListener('click', function () {
state.playing = !state.playing;
playButton.textContent = state.playing ? 'Pause angle animation' : 'Play angle animation';
if (state.playing) requestAnimationFrame(animate);
});
function animate(time) {
if (!state.playing) return;
if (!state.lastTime) state.lastTime = time;
const delta = Math.min(40, time - state.lastTime);
state.lastTime = time;
state.angle = 90 + Math.sin(time * 0.0012) * 90;
angleInput.value = state.angle.toFixed(0);
updateText();
draw();
requestAnimationFrame(animate);
if (delta &lt; 0) state.lastTime = time;
}
let dragging = false;
let lastX = 0;
let lastY = 0;
canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', function (event) {
dragging = true;
lastX = event.clientX;
lastY = event.clientY;
canvas.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
});
canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', function (event) {
if (!dragging) return;
state.yaw += (event.clientX - lastX) * 0.008;
state.pitch = Math.max(-1.2, Math.min(1.2, state.pitch + (event.clientY - lastY) * 0.008));
lastX = event.clientX;
lastY = event.clientY;
draw();
});
canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', function () {
dragging = false;
});
canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', function () {
dragging = false;
});
canvas.addEventListener('wheel', function (event) {
event.preventDefault();
state.zoom = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.5, state.zoom - event.deltaY * 0.001));
draw();
}, { passive: false });
window.addEventListener('resize', resize);
updateText();
resize();
}());
&lt;/script>
&lt;style>
